over the course of its motion through the galaxy , our solar system has encountered many interstellar environments of varying characteristics . interstellar medium ( ism ) density variations spanning seven orders of magnitude are commonly seen throughout the general galactic environment , and a sufficiently dense cloud within this range has the potential to dramatically alter the structure of the heliosphere . we present observations of the ism environments the sun has most recently encountered based on high - resolution optical spectra toward nearby stars in the direction of the historical solar trajectory . this survey of interstellar matter toward nearby young stars within their birthplace highlights how ism conditions can have profound effects on space weather throughout a galaxy . we show how variations in ism density can be traced all the way out to the outer boundaries of the solar system.
